+
+### Ocean drift inputs
+
+`crates/ocean` carries floating objects with the surface current, Stokes drift and
+10 m wind (`mh370 drift`, configs in `config/ocean.toml` and `config/drift/`). Its
+inputs are too large for git and live in `data/external/ocean/`
+(`/jackbox/home/MH370-inputs`). Each file has a `.json` sidecar with its sources and
+sha256, and is rebuilt by a script in `.sources/ocean-drift/`. The MHGRID and MHLAND
+layouts are documented in `crates/ocean/src/field.rs` and `land.rs`.
+
+| File | Content | Source |
+|---|---|---|
+| `glorys12/glorys12-surface-currents.mhgrid` | Surface (0.494 m) current, 1/12°, daily means stamped 12:00 UTC, 0–180°E × 55°S–15°N, 2014-03-07 to 2017-01-31 (7.7 GB) | CMEMS GLOBAL_MULTIYEAR_PHY_001_030 (GLORYS12V1); `cmems.py` |
+| `waverys/waverys-stokes.mhgrid` | Surface Stokes drift, 0.2°, 3-hourly, same domain and period | CMEMS GLOBAL_MULTIYEAR_WAV_001_032 (WAVERYS); `cmems.py` |
+| `oscar2/oscar2-currents-20140307-20160831.mhgrid` | Total current averaged over the top 30 m (geostrophic + Ekman + buoyancy), 0.25°, daily, 0–180°E × 55°S–15°N. Near-shore cells OSCAR leaves undefined on some days count as its coast | NASA PO.DAAC OSCAR v2.0 Final (doi:10.5067/OSCAR-25F20), Earthdata login; `oscar.py` |
+| `bran2016/bran2016-currents-20140307-20160831.mhgrid` | Surface (2.5 m) current, 0.1°, daily, 20–150°E × 55°S–5°N; BRAN2016 ends in August 2016 | CSIRO Bluelink BRAN2016 via NCI OPeNDAP, free with acknowledgement; `bran.py` |
+| `era5-wind10/era5-wind10-*.mhgrid` | 10 m wind: 0.25° hourly for March–May 2014, and 0.5° 3-hourly for 2014-03-07 to 2016-08-31 | ECMWF ERA5 original daily files in the public ARCO bucket; `era5_wind.py` |
+| `gshhg/gshhg-f-land-30s.mhland` | Land at 30″ (≈0.9 km), 0–180°E × 55°S–15°N | GSHHG 2.3.7 full resolution (LGPL); `gshhg_land.py` |
+| `gdp/gdp_6hour_20{14,15,16}.csv` | Drifter positions every 6 h with drogue-loss times, 30–115°E × 50°S–5°N | NOAA Global Drifter Program |
+
+Two departures from how these inputs were used before:
+- **Strong currents.** The previous GLORYS12 conversion let netCDF4 mask values outside
+  each file's valid_min/valid_max, so currents beyond −1.91/+2.63 m/s (the Agulhas and
+  Somali currents) became missing. `cmems.py` treats only `_FillValue` as missing.
+- **Time stamps.** Daily means are stamped at 12:00 UTC, the centre of the averaged day,
+  not at 00:00.
